nd a little I  don't know braggadocious if you say yeah  I did the math and I'm gonna be 38 when  I break the record so I what is it  about the passing numbers now is it more  about what the offense quarterbacks are  doing or what the defense is not doing I  think the combination of both you know I  think there's some really great  quarterback play in the league right now  you know young guys the old guys I mean  it's all over the place what Pat mahomes  is doing all the way up to you know drew  and Tom still playing at a really high  level so it's it's a really good era for  quarterbacks I think in the NFL right  now and at the same time there are some  things that you know probably you know  helping offenses be a little bit more  prolific and I think it's for the better  of the game just because all of it  really is intended to keep guys safe and  keep you guys playing for as long as  they can which is ultimately what we all  want to do you know we want to play this  game as long as we can and have fun  doing it but also if you're looking at  this the way the game is now - when you  first came in how much of a difference  is it for offense and defense in your  your opinion I think it's changed quite  a bit really in all phases you know  obviously you know rules are different  for defenders now than they were back in  2009 when I came in all the Egan and  like I said earlier I think it's for the  right reasons and I think you know some  of it is tough you know it's tough to  officiate I think it's tough for certain  guys that have played for a long time to  kind of have to change the way they play  the game but I think it'll keep you guys  safe keep you guys healthy and keep it  playing longer and then offensive ly  schemes are constantly changing you know  and some of these skill players that are  coming out now are just incredible  incredible athletes big tall faster on  all of it so it's it's a really cool  time to be playing in the NFL and I  enjoy playing he's